  "query_preview": "..(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 226 AM EDT SAT OCT 3 2026\n\nA cold front will be moving south across the area to begin the\nperiod Sunday evening, bringing a prolonged stretch of dry \nweather lasting through the upcoming week. \n\nMonday will see the return to calm and quiet conditions across the \nregion. High pressure will build across the Great Lakes, before \nmigrating further east with time. A second high pressure system \nwill then build in across the Ohio Valley, sustaining our dry \nweather through Friday with plentiful sunshine expected. Highs \neach day through the week should be mostly in the 70s, with a few \n80s returning to our southwest counties as early as Thursday. \nLows, especially on Monday and Tuesday nights, do look to be \npretty chilly in the lower 40s. A few sheltered valleys could dip \ninto the upper 30s, although model guidance does not really \nsupport frost quite yet, with fog a better possibility in the \nriver valleys.",
